<UserControl x:Class="MonitorBrightnessController.Presentation.HelpTab"
             xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             xmlns:d="http://schemas.microsoft.com/expression/blend/2008"
             xmlns:mc="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/markup-compatibility/2006"
             mc:Ignorable="d">
    <ScrollViewer VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto" Padding="12">
        <StackPanel Margin="12">

            <!-- Section: Monitor Brightness & Gamma Control -->
            <TextBlock Text="Monitor Brightness &amp; Gamma Control"
                       FontWeight="Bold" FontSize="15"
                       Margin="0,0,0,4" />
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Margin="0,0,0,16">
                Adjust the brightness and gamma of each connected monitor individually using sliders or numeric text input.
                Values range from 0 to 100. Changes are applied immediately via DDC/CI when you release the slider
                or press Enter in the text field. If a monitor does not support DDC/CI, an error message is displayed
                next to its controls.
            </TextBlock>

            <!-- Section: Profiles -->
            <TextBlock Text="Profiles"
                       FontWeight="Bold" FontSize="15"
                       Margin="0,0,0,4" />
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Margin="0,0,0,16">
                Save your current brightness and gamma settings as a named profile for quick recall.
                Use "Save As New" to create a profile or delete profiles you no longer need.
                A default startup profile can be configured in Settings to automatically apply on silent launch.
            </TextBlock>

            <!-- Section: Profile Preview -->
            <TextBlock Text="Profile Preview"
                       FontWeight="Bold" FontSize="15"
                       Margin="0,0,0,4" />
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Margin="0,0,0,16">
                Selecting a profile from the Monitors tab dropdown previews its brightness and gamma values
                in the sliders without sending any commands to your monitors. Click the "Apply" button to
                send the previewed values to your hardware. Clear the dropdown selection to restore the sliders
                to the current live hardware values. Legacy profiles without gamma data leave gamma sliders unchanged.
            </TextBlock>

            <!-- Section: Smooth Transitions -->
            <TextBlock Text="Smooth Transitions"
                       FontWeight="Bold" FontSize="15"
                       Margin="0,0,0,4" />
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Margin="0,0,0,16">
                When applying a profile, brightness and gamma values transition smoothly over a short duration
                rather than changing abruptly. This provides a comfortable visual experience, especially when
                switching between profiles with large differences in brightness or gamma values.
            </TextBlock>

            <!-- Section: System Tray Behavior -->
            <TextBlock Text="System Tray Behavior"
                       FontWeight="Bold" FontSize="15"
                       Margin="0,0,0,4" />
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Margin="0,0,0,16">
                When minimized, the application resides in the system tray (notification area).
                Double-click the tray icon to restore the main window. Right-click the tray icon
                for a context menu with options to show the window or exit the application.
                The application continues running in the background while minimized to tray.
            </TextBlock>

            <!-- Section: Startup Behavior -->
            <TextBlock Text="Startup Behavior"
                       FontWeight="Bold" FontSize="15"
                       Margin="0,0,0,4" />
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Margin="0,0,0,16">
                When launched manually (without flags), the application reads your monitors' current hardware
                brightness and gamma values and displays them in the sliders. No profile is applied automatically.
                When launched in silent mode (--silent), the application applies your configured startup profile
                and stays minimized to the system tray. CLI flags such as --monitor or --profile override the
                startup profile and execute only the specified command.
            </TextBlock>

            <!-- Section: Start with Windows -->
            <TextBlock Text="Start with Windows"
                       FontWeight="Bold" FontSize="15"
                       Margin="0,0,0,4" />
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Margin="0,0,0,16">
                Toggle "Start with Windows" in Settings to create or remove the auto-start registry entry.
                When enabled, the application launches in silent mode on login and applies your startup profile.
                This toggle works seamlessly with the installer's "Start with Windows" option — both manage
                the same registry entry. If the installer created the entry, the application detects it on
                next launch and syncs the setting automatically.
            </TextBlock>

            <!-- Section: CLI Usage -->
            <TextBlock Text="CLI Usage"
                       FontWeight="Bold" FontSize="15"
                       Margin="0,0,0,4" />
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Margin="0,0,0,16">
                The application supports command-line arguments for scripting and automation.
                Use --monitor &lt;index&gt; --brightness &lt;value&gt; --gamma &lt;value&gt; to set
                a specific monitor's values directly. Use --profile &lt;name&gt; to apply a saved profile.
                Multiple --monitor groups can be specified in a single command. The application exits
                after executing CLI commands without showing a window.
            </TextBlock>

            <!-- Section: Silent Startup Mode -->
            <TextBlock Text="Silent Startup Mode"
                       FontWeight="Bold" FontSize="15"
                       Margin="0,0,0,4" />
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Margin="0,0,0,16">
                Launch the application with the --silent argument to start without displaying the main window.
                The application minimizes directly to the system tray and applies the configured startup profile
                (either the default profile or the last-used profile). If no profile is configured, no values
                are applied. CLI flags (--monitor, --profile) override the startup profile when combined with
                --silent. This mode is used automatically when "Start with Windows" is enabled.
            </TextBlock>

            <!-- Section: Auto-Update Notifications -->
            <TextBlock Text="Auto-Update Notifications"
                       FontWeight="Bold" FontSize="15"
                       Margin="0,0,0,4" />
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Margin="0,0,0,16">
                On startup, the application checks for newer versions on GitHub. If a new version is available,
                a notification banner appears at the top of the window with a link to the release page.
                You can dismiss the notification or disable update checks entirely in Settings.
                The application never downloads or installs updates automatically.
            </TextBlock>

            <!-- Section: Shortcut Creation -->
            <TextBlock Text="Shortcut Creation"
                       FontWeight="Bold" FontSize="15"
                       Margin="0,0,0,4" />
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Margin="0,0,0,16">
                The installer can create Start Menu and Desktop shortcuts during setup. You can also create
                profile-specific shortcuts from within the application — these launch the app and immediately
                apply the chosen profile, which is useful for quick-switch scenarios or taskbar pins.
            </TextBlock>

            <!-- Section: Installation & Updates -->
            <TextBlock Text="Installation &amp; Updates"
                       FontWeight="Bold" FontSize="15"
                       Margin="0,0,0,4" />
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Margin="0,0,0,16">
                Monitor Brightness Controller is installed via an Inno Setup installer. The installer places
                the application in Program Files, creates optional Start Menu and Desktop shortcuts, and can
                configure "Start with Windows" during setup. Upgrading to a new version preserves your settings,
                shortcuts, and startup preferences — simply run the new installer over the existing installation.
                Uninstalling removes installed files, shortcuts, and the auto-start registry entry.
            </TextBlock>

        </StackPanel>
    </ScrollViewer>
</UserControl>
